{"id": "g3_distinct_small_residue_five_count", "signature": "solve(samples)", "statement": "Given a list of integers `samples`, count how many DISTINCT values v in it satisfy 1 <= v <= 100 and v % 6 == 5 (Python's % operator, so the remainder is always in 0..5). Repeated values are counted once. Zero, negative values, and values above 100 are never counted. Return 0 if there are none, including for an empty list.", "tests": [{"args": [[]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[3]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[3, 3, 3]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[-1, -5, 3, 7, 11]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[101, 107, 5]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[5, 11, 17, 23, 5, 11]], "expected": 4}, {"args": [[0, 6, 12, -7, -1]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[1, 2, 3, 4]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[100, 95, 89]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[5, 5, -11, 11, 65]], "expected": 3}, {"args": [[-8, 2, 14, 40, -19, 63, 83, 51, -18, -14]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[35]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[15, 23, 59, 14]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[-20, 41, 109, -19, -1]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[108, 103, 112, 39, 31, -2, 73, 86, 119]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[-1, 20, 86, 2, 52, 24]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[80, 91, 33, 95, 39, 61, -6, 34, -12, 95, -6]], "expected": 1}], "facts": [["arg", "samples", "int_list"], ["iterate", "samples"], ["bound", "ge", "1"], ["bound", "le", "100"], ["remainder", "6", "5"], ["distinct", "original"], ["aggregate", "count"], ["size", "samples", "tiny"]], "deps": {"schema": ["seq_fold"], "uses": [], "solution_sha256": "549b7ab1a35d3c26b2f054f490ae2e90fa4aac534f99d51fb29cce0cab79dfa7", "reference_sha256": "c315aecf431ae1e8eb85360324db36408fe5784fa30150f1a12a067065bcd0a9"}}